Script factory value-initialisation (campaign full audits 2026-10-07).

Several mission scripts read members before Created() or a custom event
assigns them (M01 controller ids, M05 poke index, M11 Sydney conversation ids,
M13 area-4 controller ids, M09 innate zone flag ...). The scripts are created
with new T, so those members hold leftover heap contents; on Vita the 12+
campaign sessions reuse one process heap, so stale conversation ids (which
restart at 1000 every level) can match live ones. DECLARE_SCRIPT classes have
no user-provided default constructor, so new T() zero-initialises the whole
object before the implicit constructor runs. Valid-path behaviour is
unchanged; members a script assigns are overwritten as before.

--- a/ScriptRegistrant.h
+++ b/ScriptRegistrant.h
@@ -49,7 +49,12 @@
 
 		virtual ScriptImpClass* Create(void)
 			{
-			T* script = new T;
+			// Vita port: value-initialise. DECLARE_SCRIPT classes have no user-provided
+			// constructor, so new T() zero-fills members a script reads before
+			// assigning (ids, counters, conversation handles) instead of leaving
+			// whatever a previous mission's session left in the reused heap. Loaded
+			// scripts still restore their saved variables after Create().
+			T* script = new T();
 			assert(script != NULL);
 			script->SetFactory(this);
 			script->Register_Auto_Save_Variables();
